<Layout title="The First Harvest">
  <article>

    <h1>The First Harvest</h1>

    <p><em>26 July 2026</em></p>

    <img
  src="/images/journal/2026-07-26/FenuGreek-2.jpg"
  alt="Fenugreek seedlings continuing to grow"
  style="width:100%;max-width:700px;border-radius:8px;margin:2rem 0;"
/>

    <p>
      Today the garden found its way into our kitchen, yet again
    </p>

    <p>
      While this is not new, this was first one after I started logging every day, this project got created yesterday. Today, I am in a position to log every day, but this was my first log. 
    </p>

    <p>
      The harvest was a bowl of young <strong>fenugreek (menthya)</strong>
      seedlings grown from seed. They were harvested fresh and became part
      of the sambar prepared for our family.
    </p>

    <p>
      It wasn't a large harvest. It wasn't meant to be.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every productive garden begins with moments like this.
      Today the garden completed its first cycle:
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      Seed → Plant → Harvest → Meal
    </blockquote>

    <p>
      This journal exists to remember those moments.
    </p>

    <img
  src="/images/journal/2026-07-26/FenuGreek-1.jpg"
  alt="Fenugreek seedlings continuing to grow"
  style="width:100%;max-width:700px;border-radius:8px;margin:2rem 0;"
/>

    <h2>Garden Notes</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Crop:</strong> Fenugreek (Menthya)</li>
      <li><strong>Harvest:</strong> Young seedlings</li>
      <li><strong>Use:</strong> Fresh greens used in sambar</li>
      <li><strong>Significance:</strong> First edible produce from the Bangalore Grower garden</li>
    </ul>

  </article>
